{
  "dom_id": "step-q128408",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$(-4)\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-3)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive: \n\n$$\n(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{(-4)\\cdot (-4)}_{⏟}}_{16}\\cdot (-3)=16\\cdot (-3).\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a positive times a negative gives a negative:\n\n$$\n16\\cdot (-3)=-(16\\cdot 3)=-48\n$$",
